  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the two lotteries and deems probability differences negligible. It then prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher) maximum outcome. Here, Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 2400 Euros with 100% probability, while Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 2500 Euros with 33% probability. Thus, the maximum outcome of B (2500) is higher than that of A (2400). The probability distributions differ substantially: A offers certainty, while B involves risk with 33%, 66%, and 1% probabilities. However, the reason explicitly treats such probability differences as negligible. Therefore, according to the reason, B should be preferred due to its higher maximum outcome, assuming the individual disregards the probability differences.",
