  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) treating probability differences as negligible and (2) preferring the lottery with the higher maximum outcome. However, the individual did not treat probability differences as negligible—they gave central importance to the certainty of 2400 in A versus the uncertainty in B. Moreover, although the individual acknowledged that B has a higher maximum outcome (2500), they did not use this as a reason to prefer B; instead, they dismissed it due to the small difference and the risk involved. The individual’s justification is based on risk avoidance and preference for certainty, which contradicts the core logic of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual did not apply the reason. The relevant information (maximum outcomes) was considered, but not in the way the reason prescribes, and the rule of the reason (prefer higher maximum when probabilities are negligible) was not followed.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

