  "step_3": "The decision reason requires two components: (1) treating the probability difference as negligible, and (2) choosing based on the more favorable maximum outcome. The individual does acknowledge that the 0.1% difference is very small and likely inconsequential, satisfying the first component. However, instead of switching focus to the maximum outcome, they explicitly justify their choice based on preferring the higher probability (0.2% > 0.1%), which contradicts the second component of the reason. The reason would prefer Lottery B due to its higher maximum outcome, but the individual chose Lottery A due to its higher probability. Therefore, although the individual noticed the similarity in probabilities, they did not use the rule of preferring the higher outcome when probabilities are negligible. Instead, they used a probability-maximizing heuristic. The verbal report shows awareness of the relevant factors but applies a different decision rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
